/Kafka
We have 1 consumer group with 2 instances of one service and topic from some producer with 3 partitions.
How partitions weill be read?
- some instance will get messages from two partitions another instance - from one partitions
What if 3 instances and 2 partition
- then one instance is useless in messages reading, only two services will read every with 1 partition
How can we set up Kafka to read messages in order of sending, one by one? 10:20
- using keys for messages we want to read in order, then all of them will get in same partition in order of sending
- If you need order for ALL messages in topic, not just for one key group — you need topic with 1 partition only.
We want our events to be consumed exactly one time, how to set it up? where? in consumer or producer side? 11:05
- Exactly-once needs setup on producer AND consumer side. Producer side:
- enable.idempotence=true — stops duplicate messages if producer retries
- Use Kafka transactions if you write to few partitions/topics and need all-or-nothing @Transactional("kafkaTransactionManager")
- Consumer side: isolation.level=read_committed — consumer will read only committed messages

