We have some rest endpoint returning user by id. At some point we see that its latency growth up a lot, how to analyze it? 15:00
- in postgresql there is extension pg_stat_statements, we set it up and check which requests and mostly used and its avg executing time
- there we see all the slowest queries related to our user selecting and use EXPLAIN on them, it shown us query plan
- there we are looking for sequential scans through the tables, if there are join - highly likely there are unindexed foreign keys

Imagine that 90% of our selects in DB are same queries for 20% of rows in DB. What can we do to optimize selection in such case?
- add cache, for many instances best option is Redis, store queries as keys and responses as values, set up removing after some time
